+class AdmittanceTracker:
+    """Follows the resonance from each comparable CONTROL sample (review/32).
+
+    The sample's port admittance, de-embedded with the estimated C0, gives the
+    motional R + jX at the held point. When it is off the model's prediction
+    by more than admittance_model_tolerance (or noise_sigmas times the measured
+    sample-to-sample scatter of Y, if larger), the estimate is updated from it:
+    Rm and fs, and Lm from the previous held point as well when the two are at
+    least admittance_min_separation_per_width widths apart. A predicted
+    soft-feasible gain above admittance_move_gain then moves the held point to
+    the model's optimum at once, without probes. k, the measured over predicted
+    port voltage per unit drive, is refreshed when it is off by the same
+    tolerance. While k is off 1 by more than the tolerance, the declared
+    network does not explain the port voltage and the model does not know where
+    that has put the optimum (network): it neither moves the point nor explains
+    a level change, and the power monitor, P&O and the capture are in charge;
+    k coming back to 1 (the declared network again) gives the model back. A
+    model move the next measurement shows to be worse is undone by the caller
+    (suspended) until P&O parks by itself, a capture or recall lands, or the
+    load changes again. The prior is the design file's BVD; the first sample
+    may move to the prior's optimum.
+
+    Memory: the estimate of each load that ends (the design prior first, never
+    evicted, then memory_size more) is kept. When a held point shows a new
+    load, the sample is first compared with every remembered estimate; one
+    that predicts it within the tolerance is taken as it is, without a probe
+    or an update, and the point moves straight to its optimum. A load that
+    comes back is then one move away, also when the last load had misled a
+    one-point update (its Lm).
+    """
+
+    def __init__(self, cfg: dict):
+        self.cfg = cfg
+        self.plant = AM.PlantModel(cfg, AM.design_prior())
+        self.points = []     # (frequency, Y): latest comparable sample per held point of this load, newest last
+        self.d = []          # relative |dY| of consecutive same-point, same-amplitude samples
+        self.prev = None
+        self.moves = 0
