+    """ADMITTANCE_TRACK: CAPTURE_PO with the admittance model in front (review/32).
+
+    Every comparable CONTROL sample goes to the AdmittanceTracker first. A
+    resonance that moved is followed at once (MOVE): the drive is lowered first
+    when the model predicts less headroom at the new point (prepare_move), and
+    the power reference is relearnt there with the predicted level as its prior.
+    The first comparable sample at the new point is checked against the one
+    before the move: worse by more than po_move_threshold (or noise_sigmas
+    measured difference sigmas) undoes the move, suspends model moves and
+    starts P&O at the old point. A level the model explains (EXPLAINED: Rm, or
+    a peak that only became lower) relearns the reference instead of starting a
+    capture that could find nothing better. A changed network (k) starts P&O at
+    once. Everything else is CAPTURE_PO unchanged: the power monitor, the memory
+    recall, P&O, and the capture, which also runs when the model is LOST and
+    refits the BVD from its points. Captures and their failures use the same
